{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nParis keeps its promise. We drove to the abattoir today; the machinery of death here is as organized as life, a stark reminder of necessity. We also visited the Bourse, where money dances, and Montmartre, from which the city stretches out like a vast, breathing body. The Palace of the Deputies stands firm, a symbol of the ethical state actualized in law.\n\nDinner was lively with Cousin and Fauriel. Fauriel’s Greek folk songs are charming, though he speaks of them as curiosities rather than the soul of a people. I have also enjoyed Mignet and Thiers; their history is sharp, though perhaps too much concerned with events and not enough with spirit.\n\nI think of you and the boys constantly. The air is thick with history, but my heart remains in Berlin. Write soon.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080521,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":191,"prompt_tokens":957,"total_tokens":1148,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-rlibcl0nkn58pz60mHnGujXWo9pBsBEc","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":957,"prompt_ms":968.16,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0116614420062695,"prompt_per_second":988.4729796727814,"predicted_n":191,"predicted_ms":4592.57,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.171421052631576,"predicted_per_second":41.371171261407014}}